<title>USA: Sprint launches U.S./Europe Internet link.</title>
<headline>Sprint launches U.S./Europe Internet link.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sprint Corp said Monday it has initiated a high-speed Internet link between the United States and Europe.</p>
<p>The link operates at 155 megabits per second and carries Internet traffic between the Sprint Network Access Point in Pennsauken, New Jersey, and a Tele2 node in Stockholm, Sweden.</p>
<p>Sprint said the link will result in improved responsiveness and speed for Internet Service Providers, corporations, academic organizations and government agencies.</p>
<p>Sprint provides Internet backbone and access services, long-distance phone service and other communications products.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
